{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24939-society-for-prevention-of-cruelty-to-mutants-making-hellhound-less-cruel-to-target","id":24939,"title":"Society for Prevention of Cruelty to Mutants: Making Hellhound Less Cruel to Target","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-06T23:04:15-08:00","id":24939,"title":"Society for Prevention of Cruelty to Mutants: Making Hellhound Less Cruel to Target","content":"Anyway, while I love the idea of the Hellhound exploit, I'm also an animal lover and find the idea of cryptids produced by soon starving to death something that kind of makes it <i>verboten</i> for me. I also want to be able to play a demon who fell because he developed a fondness for cryptid pets, and I don't see him creating a cryptid purely as a disposable thug, because, well...pet owner.<br /> <br /> So, while I have little problem with the Exploit, how would you make a version that results in the cryptid version of a Familiar merit? Do I just tack a Willpower dot on the normal Exploit to symbolize the demon splicing a bit of himself off to stabilize the Hellhound's mutations?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T23:36:04-08:00","id":24956,"title":"","content":"Whoa. Cryptid familiars. Can we make this a thing?!<br /> <br /> They could even have, like .. a &quot;cover&quot; of some kind, perhaps?<br /> <br /> Is that a good idea? Or am I crazy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1009-kristastic","name":"Kristastic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1009_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T23:49:17-08:00","id":24963,"title":"","content":"This now has to be a thing. Saboteur veterinarian changing the neighborhood pets into something decidedly other and sending them home with GM targets. Or the reverse being a Guardian who doesn't have the heart to put animals down and building up a menagerie of domestic and exotic animals.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> Noah's Ark.</div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/257-calrabjohns","name":"Calrabjohns","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T10:55:06-08:00","id":25242,"title":"","content":"Maybe instead of killing the pet, the transformation has to be sustained by repeated uses of the Exploit, kind of like how spirits can claim people who have been repeatedly possessed. That way, the demon can have his Cover's normal looking pet that can then be powered up.<br /> After enough use (number 